{"provider":"COURSERA","source_id":"6","coursera_id":"6","source_file":"adobe-marketing-specialist.html","workload":"10 hours per week","about":"Kick-start your marketing career with this hands-on certificate program. Designed for aspiring marketing specialists, this course covers digital marketing strategy, brand identity, content planning, and campaign performance analysis. You’ll gain practical experience with Adobe tools and walk away with a polished portfolio and certificate to prove your skills. No experience necessary. Three-month free trial offer included.","overview":["Launch your career in marketing.","Build job-ready skills in digital marketing, content development, branding, and social media."],"languages":["English"],"partners":[],"related_courses":[],"specializations":[],"level":"BEGINNER","no_of_courses":5,"total_enrollments":25142,"review":"4.7","rating":3510,"skills":["Adobe Express","Advertising","Campaign Management","Content Scheduling","Content Strategy","Cross-Channel Marketing","Data-Driven Marketing","Digital Marketing","Digital Marketing Campaigns","Generative AI","Graphic Design","Logo Design","Market Research","Marketing Planning","Marketing Strategies","Personalized Campaigns","Promotional Strategies","Responsible AI","Social Media Content","Social Media Marketing","Conversion Funnel Analysis","Marketing Materials","Marketing Strategy and Techniques","Marketing Effectiveness","Promotional Materials","Diversity Marketing","Driving engagement","Target Audience","Marketing Automation","Customer Relationship Management","Lead Generation","Promotions and Campaigns","Product Promotion","Social Media Strategy","Social Media Analytics","Regulation and Legal Compliance","Branding","Social Media","Content Creation","Intellectual Property","Visual Storytelling","Multimedia","Ethical Standards And Conduct","Drive Engagement","AI powered creativity","Social Media Management","AI Personalization","Data-Driven Decision-Making","Content Marketing","Marketing Analytics","Content Development and Management","Content Performance Analysis","Integrated Marketing Communications","Data Ethics","Marketing Channel","Adobe Firefly","Color Theory","Typography","Graphic and Visual Design Software","Usability","User Interface and User Experience (UI/UX) Design","Design Software","Generative AI Agents","Artificial Intelligence","Visual Design","Collaborative Software","Creative Design","Digital Design","Layout Design","Prompt Engineering","Image Quality","Verification And Validation","AI literacy","Creativity","AI Integrations","AI Workflows"],"offered_by":"Adobe","qualifying_job_titles":[],"at_a_glance":[],"deadlines":[],"faqs":[{"question":"1 - What is included in the field of Marketing?","answer":"1 - Marketing is a diverse and dynamic field that brings together creativity, strategy, and data to connect products, services, or brands with the right audience. It includes a variety of specializations, such as: Content marketing:  Crafting and sharing valuable content like articles, videos, and podcasts to engage audiences and build trust. Digital marketing:  Promoting products and services through online channels like social media, search engines, websites, and email campaigns. Market research:  Collecting and analyzing data on consumers, competitors, and trends to shape effective marketing strategies. SEO (Search Engine Optimization) : Enhancing website visibility on search engines through optimization techniques to attract more visitors. Social media marketing:  Building brand awareness, fostering engagement, and connecting with audiences through platforms like Instagram, LinkedIn, and TikTok. Brand management:  Shaping and maintaining a brand’s identity, values, and reputation to ensure consistency and trust. With its wide-ranging focus areas, marketing offers opportunities to make a measurable impact in nearly every industry."},{"question":"2 - What does a Marketing Specialist do?","answer":"2 - A marketing specialist wears many hats, blending creativity with analytical skills to promote a brand, product, or service effectively. In this role, you’ll use data, creativity, and technology to craft impactful marketing strategies. Your day-to-day tasks might include: - Delivering compelling advertising campaigns inspired by deep customer insights. - Conducting market research to uncover new opportunities and trends. - Collaborating with cross-functional teams to ensure cohesive and effective strategies. - Analyzing campaign performance to refine and optimize future marketing efforts. This dynamic role allows you to balance strategic thinking with hands-on execution, driving measurable results and making a meaningful impact on your organization’s success."},{"question":"3 - What background knowledge is necessary?","answer":"3 - To succeed in marketing, you’ll need a mix of foundational knowledge, technical skills, and a creative mindset. Here are some key areas to focus on: - Marketing principles:  It’s essential to understand concepts like branding, market segmentation, consumer behavior, and the marketing funnel. - Communication skills:  Strong written and verbal communication abilities are crucial for crafting compelling messages and collaborating with teams. - Analytical skills : A basic understanding of data analysis and tools like Google Analytics will help you evaluate campaign performance and make data-driven decisions. - Digital marketing tools:  It’s valuable to have hands-on experience with platforms like Adobe Express, social media management tools, SEO software, and email marketing platforms. - Creativity:  In this field, it’s highly desirable to be able to think creatively and develop innovative strategies or campaigns. - Adaptability:  Marketing trends and technologies evolve quickly, so a willingness to learn and adapt is essential. Keep in mind that you don’t need prior expertise to complete this course. Whether you’re just starting out or switching careers, the program will give you the foundation, skills, and knowledge you need to thrive in a marketing role."},{"question":"4 - Is this course really 100% online? Do I need to attend any classes in person?","answer":"4 - This course is completely online, so there’s no need to show up to a classroom in person. You can access your lectures, readings and assignments anytime and anywhere via the web or your mobile device."},{"question":"5 - Can I just enroll in a single course?","answer":"5 - Yes! To get started, click the course card that interests you and enroll. You can enroll and complete the course to earn a shareable certificate. When you subscribe to a course that is part of a Certificate, you’re automatically subscribed to the full Certificate. Visit your learner dashboard to track your progress."}],"testimonials":[],"curriculum":[{"title":"Design Fundamentals with AI","description":""},{"title":"Generative AI Content Creation","description":""},{"title":"Digital Marketing","description":""},{"title":"Social Media Content and Strategy","description":""},{"title":"Multichannel Content Marketing","description":""}],"faculty":[{"name":"Adobe"}],"description":"Unlock the fundamental design and AI skills behind high-impact digital content. In this introductory course, you’ll learn how to bring your ideas to life using Adobe Express, the design app that makes it quick and easy to ideate and create with features powered by Adobe Firefly generative AI. 

You’ll also explore design principles from typography and layout to color theory and composition, and you’ll learn how to use these principles in real-world applications such as social media posts, brand assets, and visual storytelling. 

By the end of this design fundamentals course, you’ll be ready to transform your creative concepts into polished and engaging content. Start building your foundation in content creation that supports your personal and professional goals!","tuition_cost":"₹1906 / month"}

{"provider":"COURSERA","source_id":"82","coursera_id":"82","source_file":"google-cloud-data-analytics-certificate.html","workload":"10 hours per week","about":"Become a data-driven powerhouse with Google Cloud! As a Cloud Data Analyst, you'll unlock insights hidden within vast datasets, transforming raw numbers into impactful stories that shape business strategies across the globe. This certificate program is your launchpad – a carefully curated mix of expert instruction and real-world challenges. You'll build a portfolio of impressive projects, showcasing to employers that you can analyze, visualize, and communicate data.

In this certificate program you’ll immerse yourself in the fundamentals of cloud data analytics. You’ll progressively build your working knowledge of how to structure, store, access, and visualize data using various Cloud tools and integration, such as Cloud Storage, BigQuery, Looker and Dataproc. The program will also touch on how AI is revolutionizing data analytics, from automating repetitive tasks to uncovering hidden insights.

No prior experience or degree is required to get started. This is where your journey begins – get ready to wield the tools and strategies that turn data into decisive action.","overview":["Launch your career in Cloud Data Analytics","Build in-demand skills and gain credentials to go from beginner to job-ready in 10 weeks or less. No degree or prior experience required."],"languages":["English"],"partners":[],"related_courses":[],"specializations":[],"level":"BEGINNER","no_of_courses":5,"total_enrollments":25776,"review":"4.5","rating":303,"skills":["Cloud Infrastructure","Cloud Storage","Dashboard","Dashboard Creation","Data Architecture","Data Governance","Data Infrastructure","Data Lakes","Data Management","Data Pipelines","Data Presentation","Data Storytelling","Data Visualization Software","Gemini","Google Gemini","Identity and Access Management","Interactive Data Visualization","Looker (Software)","Responsible AI","Data Visualization","Data Analysis","AI literacy","Generative AI","Data Ethics","Professional Development","Google Cloud Platform","Analytical Skills","Large Language Modeling","Problem Solving","Data Transformation","Data Cleansing","SQL","Data Collection","Extract, Transform, Load","Data Validation","Data Integration","Cloud Security","Data Quality","Data Integrity","Data Processing","Cloud Computing","Data Manipulation","Cloud-Based Integration","Cloud Computing Architecture","Cloud Platforms","Analytics","Data Storage","Digital Transformation","Data Warehousing","Cloud Technologies","Big Data","Cloud Services","Data Structures","Public Cloud","Query Languages","Application Programming Interface (API)","Data Storage Technologies","Data Access","Database Management","Metadata Management","NoSQL","Star Schema","Performance Tuning","Data Modeling","Version Control","Business Analytics","Self Service Technologies"],"offered_by":"Google Cloud","qualifying_job_titles":[],"at_a_glance":[],"deadlines":[],"faqs":[{"question":"1 - Is this course really 100% online? Do I need to attend any classes in person?","answer":"1 - This course is completely online, so there’s no need to show up to a classroom in person. You can access your lectures, readings and assignments anytime and anywhere via the web or your mobile device."},{"question":"2 - Can I just enroll in a single course?","answer":"2 - Yes! To get started, click the course card that interests you and enroll. You can enroll and complete the course to earn a shareable certificate. When you subscribe to a course that is part of a Certificate, you’re automatically subscribed to the full Certificate. Visit your learner dashboard to track your progress."}],"testimonials":[],"curriculum":[{"title":"Introduction to Data Analytics in Google Cloud","description":""},{"title":"Data Management and Storage in the Cloud","description":""},{"title":"Data Transformation in the Cloud","description":""},{"title":"The Power of Storytelling: How to Visualize Data in the Cloud","description":""},{"title":"Put It All Together: Prepare for a Cloud Data Analyst Job","description":""}],"faculty":[{"name":"Google Cloud Training"}],"description":"Welcome learner! This is the first of five courses of the Google Cloud Data Analytics Certificate. Jump into the world of data analytics and cloud computing. Explore the data lifecycle in the cloud and gain a better understanding of the common tools used by data analysts.","tuition_cost":"₹1906 / month"}

{"provider":"COURSERA","source_id":"163","coursera_id":"163","source_file":"microsoft-account-manager-with-generative-ai.html","workload":"20 hours per week","about":"Advance your career as an Account Manager by mastering AI-driven insights and customer engagement with Microsoft Copilot. The MSFT Account Manager with Copilot Professional Certificate is designed for professionals who are ready to elevate their roles or transition into modern account management. This program combines Copilot and generative AI tools to enhance productivity, streamline workflows, and foster stronger customer relationships across various industries.

You’ll develop skills in data-driven decision-making, ethical negotiation, and real-world problem-solving while building a strong portfolio through hands-on projects. By the end, you’ll be prepared for roles such as Advanced Account Manager or Strategic Partner Manager, equipped with practical expertise in tools like Microsoft Office and CRM platforms.

A basic level of computer proficiency and experience with the Microsoft Suite is recommended. Strategic thinking, adaptability, and a passion for technology will support your success. Completing the program earns a certificate that demonstrates your ability to leverage AI for strategic account management and opens up new career opportunities.","overview":["Excel in Account Management with Microsoft AI","Elevate your career with advanced AI tools and strategic skills using Microsoft Copilot."],"languages":["English"],"partners":[],"related_courses":[],"specializations":[],"level":"ADVANCED","no_of_courses":5,"total_enrollments":2547,"review":"0","skills":["Account Management","Administrative Support","Budget Management","Consultative Approaches","Consultative Selling","Content Management","Customer Relationship Management (CRM) Software","Financial Data","Financial Management","Generative AI","Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)","Negotiation","Performance Analysis","Performance Metric","Productivity Software","Proposal Development","Responsible AI","Sales Presentations","Sales Process","Solution Selling","Data Analysis","Data Visualization Software","Power BI","Budgeting","Customer Analysis","Analytics","Financial Forecasting","Account Strategy","Microsoft Copilot","Performance Measurement","Performance Reporting","Customer Data Management","Data-Driven Decision-Making","Process Optimization","File Management","Customer Service","Customer Relationship Building","Scheduling","Verbal Communication Skills","Process Mapping","Customer experience improvement","Customer Engagement","AI Personalization","Office Administration","Customer Relationship Management","Sales","Brainstorming","Communication","Personalized Service","AI Integrations","Business Process","Microsoft 365","Project Management","Process Development","Strategic Thinking","Document Management","Information Management","Process Improvement","Ethical Standards And Conduct","Business Ethics","Prospecting and Qualification","Regulatory Requirements","Data Ethics","Information Privacy","Sales Prospecting","Personally Identifiable Information","Regulation and Legal Compliance","Contract Negotiation","Compliance Management","Loyalty Programs","Relationship Management","Relationship Building"],"offered_by":"Microsoft","qualifying_job_titles":[],"at_a_glance":[],"deadlines":[],"faqs":[{"question":"1 - What background knowledge is necessary?","answer":"1 - What background knowledge is necessary? Basic computer skills and a high school level of education are recommended for program success."},{"question":"2 - Who is this program for?","answer":"2 - Designed for professionals seeking to develop account management skills enhanced with AI tools and strategic methodologies."},{"question":"3 - Is this course really 100% online? Do I need to attend any classes in person?","answer":"3 - This course is completely online, so there’s no need to show up to a classroom in person. You can access your lectures, readings and assignments anytime and anywhere via the web or your mobile device."},{"question":"4 - Can I just enroll in a single course?","answer":"4 - Yes! To get started, click the course card that interests you and enroll. You can enroll and complete the course to earn a shareable certificate. When you subscribe to a course that is part of a Certificate, you’re automatically subscribed to the full Certificate. Visit your learner dashboard to track your progress."}],"testimonials":[],"curriculum":[{"title":"Foundations of Account Management","description":""},{"title":"Advanced Customer Relationship Management","description":""},{"title":"Data-Driven Decision Making in Account Management","description":""},{"title":"Strategic PM using GenAI for Account Managers","description":""},{"title":"Negotiation and Ethical Practices in Account Management","description":""}],"faculty":[{"name":"Microsoft"}],"description":"This foundational course sets the stage for mastering sales in the modern era by combining traditional techniques with cutting-edge AI tools. Participants will dive into the essentials of the sales process, starting with an exploration of basic sales principles, including identification of sales stages, channels, and approaches. The integration of Microsoft Copilot will be introduced as a transformative digital workflow partner that augments these traditional steps. Participants will learn to map sales processes manually and then use Copilot to enhance efficiency, comparing both methods to understand where AI adds the most value. Learners will also be introduced to communication techniques crucial for sales success, employing AI to enhance verbal and non-verbal communication skills. Personalized content creation becomes a focal point, as participants leverage AI to craft unique sales messages tailored to customer needs. Through various activities, learners will construct a foundational understanding of how AI can streamline sales operations, preparing them for more advanced applications in later courses.","tuition_cost":"₹1906 / month"}

{"provider":"COURSERA","source_id":"204","coursera_id":"204","source_file":"salesforce-sales-operations.html","workload":"10 hours per week","about":"The Salesforce economy will create more than $1 trillion in new revenue and 4.2 million jobs between 2019 and 2024. Developed in partnership with Trailhead — Salesforce's official learning platform — this certificate aims to teach you the foundational skills in Salesforce that will prepare you for a variety of entry-level sales roles, including the sales operations specialist position. This certificate is designed for beginners. No previous experience in Salesforce, sales, or CRM is necessary to be successful. Through four courses, you will learn the fundamentals of CRM, how to manage leads in Salesforce, how to manage opportunities in Salesforce, how to use Salesforce to ensure customer success, and how to effectively leverage Salesforce data through reports and dashboards.","overview":["Launch Your Career in Salesforce","Learn the foundational skills in Salesforce needed to start a new career."],"languages":["English"],"partners":[],"related_courses":[],"specializations":[],"level":"BEGINNER","no_of_courses":4,"total_enrollments":98091,"review":"4.6","rating":2558,"skills":["Closing (Sales)","Customer Relationship Management","Customer Relationship Management (CRM) Software","Customer Success Management","Dashboard","General Sales Practices","Lead Generation","Order Entry","Order Management","Request For Quotation (RFQ)","Sales","Sales Development","Sales Enablement","Sales Management","Sales Pipelines","Sales Process","Sales Support","Sales Operations","Salesforce","Service Management","Databases","Data Cleansing","Customer Data Management","Business-To-Consumer","B2B Sales","Data Management","Campaign Management","Data Entry","Prospecting and Qualification","Promotions and Campaigns","Sales Prospecting","Data Import/Export","Data-Driven Decision-Making","Business Reporting","Performance Reporting","Data Storytelling","Data Visualization","Inside Sales","Customer Service","Customer and Client Support","Customer Support","Product Knowledge","Contract Management","Product Assortment","Account Management","Order Processing","Collaborative Software","Order Management Systems","Kanban Principles","Product Lining"],"offered_by":"Salesforce","qualifying_job_titles":[],"at_a_glance":[],"deadlines":[],"faqs":[{"question":"1 - How long does it take to complete the Specialization?","answer":"1 - The entire Specialization takes 16 weeks to complete. There are four courses in the Specialization and each course takes four weeks to complete."},{"question":"2 - What background knowledge is necessary?","answer":"2 - None! This Specialization is designed for total beginners."},{"question":"3 - Do I need to take the courses in a specific order?","answer":"3 - It is recommended that you take the courses in chronological order. However, if you already have some experience in CRM or Sales — or are interested in a specific topic (i.e., Opportunity Management in Salesforce) — you are free to take the courses in whatever order you prefer."},{"question":"4 - Will I earn university credit for completing the Specialization?","answer":"4 - No university credit is offered at this time for completion of this Specialization."},{"question":"5 - What will I be able to do upon completing the Specialization?","answer":"5 - You will be able to pursue entry level sales jobs upon completion of this Specialization. Specifically, you will be in a great position to pursue the role of a sales operations specialist or a sales support specialist."},{"question":"6 - Is this course really 100% online? Do I need to attend any classes in person?","answer":"6 - This course is completely online, so there’s no need to show up to a classroom in person. You can access your lectures, readings and assignments anytime and anywhere via the web or your mobile device."},{"question":"7 - Can I just enroll in a single course?","answer":"7 - Yes! To get started, click the course card that interests you and enroll. You can enroll and complete the course to earn a shareable certificate. When you subscribe to a course that is part of a Certificate, you’re automatically subscribed to the full Certificate. Visit your learner dashboard to track your progress."}],"testimonials":[],"curriculum":[{"title":"Sales and CRM Overview","description":""},{"title":"Lead Management in Salesforce","description":""},{"title":"Opportunity Management in Salesforce","description":""},{"title":"Reports, Dashboards, and Customer Success in Salesforce","description":""}],"faculty":[{"name":"Trailhead"},{"name":"Anthony Jones"},{"name":"Angela Prakash"}],"description":"This course is the first of a series that aims to teach you the foundational skills in Salesforce that will prepare you for a variety of entry-level sales roles, including the sales operations specialist position. 

This course is designed for beginners. No previous experience in Salesforce, sales, or CRM is necessary to be successful. In this course, you will be introduced to essential concepts like the fundamentals of the sales process. You'll also learn about what Customer Relationship Management (CRM) systems are and what they are used for, you'll dive into Salesforce's main products and their use cases, and you will gain a working knowledge of the key functionalities of the Salesforce Sales Cloud that help support a business’s growth.

This course is the first step in your learning journey with Salesforce. It will provide you with the foundation you need to go into depth with more advanced Salesforce tools taught later in the certificate, and ultimately launch your new career. Please note that if you already have background knowledge in sales and CRM, or if you want to dive immediately into content that goes into more depth with Salesforce, it is recommended that you start with Course 2 in this certificate: Lead Management in Salesforce.","tuition_cost":"₹1906 / month"}
